<Placemark><name>notam-lggg/2026/A4114</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-11-05T10:29:00Z to 2026-12-11T20:59:00Z

A4114/26 NOTAMN Q) LGGG/QAFXX/IV/NBO/E /000/999/3705N02445E341 A) LGGG  PART 1 OF 3  B) 2611112100  C) 2612112059  E) NAVIGATIONAL WARNING TO ALL CONCERNED: 
REF (A) GREEK NOTAM A4071/26 (031248 EUECYIYN NOV 2026). 
REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4950/26 (041342 EUECYIYN NOV 2026). 
WITH REFERENCE TO REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4950/26 WE POINT OUT THAT 
THE ASSERTIONS CONTAINED THEREIN ARE REJECTED AS MISLEADING AND 
DEVOID OF ANY LEGAL BASIS. IN THIS RESPECT AND FURTHER TO THE REF 
(A) GREEK NOTAM A4071/26, PARA 2.2, WE REITERATE THAT GREECE, 
ESTABLISHED IN 1931 IN ACCORDANCE WITH INTERNATIONAL LAW A 
TERRITORIAL SEA OF TEN NAUTICAL MILES FOR THE PURPOSES OF AVIATION 
AND THE CONTROL THEREOF. 
THEREFORE, GREEK AIRSPACE DOES NOT EXCEED THE BREADTH OF THE 
TERRITORIAL SEA AS ESTABLISHED IN 1931. 
GREECE, THEREFORE, FULLY ABIDES BY INTERNATIONAL LAW AND WILL 
CONTINUE TO DO SO WHILE FULLY EXERCISING ITS SOVEREIGNTY. IN FACT, AS 
FAR AS INTERNATIONAL LAW IS CONCERNED, TURKIYE IS THE ONLY COUNTRY, 
REGRETTABLY, WHICH ALSO FAILS TO RESPECT THE PROVISIONS OF THE 
CHICAGO CONVENTION WITHIN THE ATHINAI FIR, WHERE, IN ACCORDANCE WITH 
THE ICAO REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATION AGREEMENTS OF 1950-1952-1958, THE 
GREEK AUTHORITIES ARE THE ONLY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES CHARGED TO 
IMPLEMENT THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF THE CHICAGO END PART 1 OF 3
A4114/26 NOTAMN Q) LGGG/QAFXX/IV/NBO/E /000/999/3705N02445E341 A) LGGG  PART 2 OF 3  B) 2611112100  C) 2612112059  E) CONVENTION AND TO 
ENSURE UNIMPEDED, REGULAR AND SAFE AIR TRAFFIC. 
ALSO, REFERENCE IS MADE TO THE ABOVE REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4950/26 
IN ORDER TO STATE THAT THE ATHINAI/ISTANBUL FIR BOUNDARY BETWEEN 
POINTS 404500N0261000E AND 360500N0300000E HAS BEEN ESTABLISHED BY 
ICAO REGIONAL AGREEMENTS (REACHED IN THE SECOND MIDDLE EAST REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATION MEETING, ISTANBUL 1950 AND SUBSEQUENTLY APPROVED BY 
THE ICAO COUNCIL ON 14 DEC 1950, DOC 7055 MID/2-RAC) WITH THE 
PARTICIPATION AND APPROVAL OF TURKIYE AND IN FEB 1958, (DOC 7870, 
EUM/IV) AND CONSEQUENTLY IS FOUNDED ON THE FIRMEST POSSIBLE LEGAL 
BASIS AS NOTED IN OUR A1709/07 LGGGYNYX NOTAM. 
FURTHERMORE THE SAID ATHINAI/ISTANBUL FIR BOUNDARY WAS DEPICTED ON 
CHART NUMBER 7 ATTACHED TO THE REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATION AGREEMENT 
WHICH WAS REACHED IN THE THIRD REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATIONAL CONFERENCE 
(PARIS 1952) AND SUBSEQUENTLY APPROVED BY THE ICAO COUNCIL ON 23 
JUNE 1952. 
ACCORDINGLY, GREECE HAS BEEN ASIGNED RESPONSIBILITY FOR ALL ATM 
SERVICES AND ICAO PURPOSES AS WELL AS FOR SAR WITHIN 
ATHINAI FIR/ HELLAS UIR AND IS THE ONLY COMPETENT THEREIN. 
FINALLY, THE ADDITIONAL PROVISION MENTIONED IN PARAGRAPH 2.3 OF 
THE REF (A) GREEK END PART 2 OF 3
A4114/26 NOTAMN Q) LGGG/QAFXX/IV/NBO/E /000/999/3705N02445E341 A) LGGG  PART 3 OF 3  B) 2611112100  C) 2612112059  E) NOTAM A4071/26 (031248 EUECYIYN NOV 2026) AIM AT 
THE PROMOTION OF SAFETY, REGULARITY AND EFFICIENCY OF INTERNATIONAL 
AIR NAVIGATION AND FOR UNMANNED AIRCRAFT IDENTIFICATION PURPOSES IN 
CONFORMITY WITH ARTICLE 3 (D) OF THE ICAO CONVENTION ON INTERNATIONAL 
CIVIL AVIATION AS AMPLIFIED BY THE A40-04 ICAO ASSEMBLY RESOLUTIONS, 
APPENDIX I, RESOLVING CLAUSE 2, SEE ALSO THE ANNEX 2, APPENDIX 4, TO 
THE ICAO CONVENTION ON INTERNATIONAL CIVIL AVIATION AS WELL AS 
ARTICLE 12 OF THE ICAO CONVENTION AND THE ESTABLISHED INTERNATIONAL 
PRACTICE. 
CONSEQUENTLY, THE POINTS RAISED BY TURKIYE IN REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM 
A4950/26 (041342 EUECYIYN NOV 2026), ARE IRRELEVANT AND THE SAID NOTAM IS NULL AND VOID AND NOT APPLICABLE TO ATHINAI FIR/ HELLAS 
UIR. THE REQUIREMENTS EXPRESSED IN THE REF (A) GREEK NOTAM 
A4071/26, ARE FULLY IN FORCE. END PART 3 OF 3</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>26.16667,40.75,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>30.0,36.08333,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>notam-lggg/2026/A4104</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-11-04T12:31:00Z to 2026-11-13T17:00:00Z

A4104/26 NOTAMN Q) LGGG/QAFXX/IV/NBO/E /000/999/3705N02445E341 A) LGGG  PART 1 OF 2  B) 2611050330  C) 2611131700  E) NAVIGATIONAL WARNING TO ALL CONCERNED: 
REF (A) GREEK NOTAM A4091/26 (040916 EUECYIYN NOV 2026). 
REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4941/26 (041159 EUECYIYN NOV 2026). 
REF (C) TURKISH NOTAM A4904/26 (021222 EUECYIYN NOV 2026). 
REFERENCE IS MADE TO THE ABOVE REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4941/26 
LTAAYNYX IN ORDER TO STATE THAT THE ATHINAI/ISTANBUL FIR BOUNDARY 
BETWEEN POINTS 404500N0261000E AND 360500N0300000E HAS BEEN 
ESTABLISHED BY ICAO REGIONAL AGREEMENTS (REACHED IN THE SECOND 
MIDDLE EAST REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATION MEETING, ISTANBUL 1950 AND 
SUBSEQUENTLY APPROVED BY THE ICAO COUNCIL ON 14 DEC 1950, DOC 7055 
MID/2-RAC) WITH THE PARTICIPATION AND APPROVAL OF TURKIYE AND IN FEB 
1958, (DOC 7870, EUM/IV) AND CONSEQUENTLY IS FOUNDED ON THE FIRMEST 
POSSIBLE LEGAL BASIS AS NOTED IN OUR A1709/07 LGGGYNYX NOTAM. 
FURTHERMORE THE SAID ATHINAI/ISTANBUL FIR BOUNDARY WAS DEPICTED ON 
CHART NUMBER 7 ATTACHED TO THE REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATION AGREEMENT 
WHICH WAS REACHED IN THE THIRD REGIONAL AIR NAVIGATIONAL CONFERENCE 
(PARIS 1952) AND SUBSEQUENTLY APPROVED BY THE ICAO COUNCIL ON 23 
JUNE 1952. 
ACCORDINGLY, GREECE HAS BEEN ASIGNED RESPONSIBILITY FOR ALL ATM 
SERVICES AND ICAO PURPOSES AS WELL AS FOR SAR END PART 1 OF 2
A4104/26 NOTAMN Q) LGGG/QAFXX/IV/NBO/E /000/999/3705N02445E341 A) LGGG  PART 2 OF 2  B) 2611050330  C) 2611131700  E) WITHIN 
ATHINAI FIR/ HELLAS UIR AND IS THE ONLY COMPETENT THEREIN. 
THEREFORE, THE DEFINITION OF EXERCISE OR SAR AREAS WITH REFERENCE 
TO THE AFOREMENTIONED ATHINAI/ISTANBUL FIR BOUNDARY, AS THIS 
BOUNDARY IS CLEARLY DEPICTED IN THE ICAO AERONAUTICAL CHARTS, IS A 
JUSTIFIED AND RIGHTFUL PRACTICE NOT LEAVING SPACE FOR MISLEADING OR 
MISINTERPRETATIONS. 
ON THE AFOREMENTIONED BASIS THE REF (A) GREEK NOTAM A4091/26 (040916 
EUECYIYN NOV 2026), STATED THAT WITH REFERENCE TO REF (C) TURKISH 
NOTAM A4904/26 (021222 EUECYIYN NOV 2026) A PART OF THE AREA AS 
DESCRIBED IN REF (A) GREEK NOTAM A4091/26, STRICTLY LIES WITHIN 
ATHINAI FIR WHERE THE ONLY COMPETENT AUTHORITY TO PROMULGATE NOTAMS 
ACCORDING TO ICAO RULES AND REGULATIONS IS THE HELLENIC AVIATION 
SERVICE PROVIDER (HASP). 
CONSEQUENTLY, THE REF (B) TURKISH NOTAM A4941/26 (041159 EUECYIYN NOV 
2026) HAS NO GROUND, CANNOT PRODUCE ANY INTERNATIONALLY LEGAL EFFECT 
WITHIN ATHINAI FIR / HELLAS UIR AND IS CONSIDERED NULL AND VOID. 
THE ONLY VALID AND EFFECTIVE NOTAM WITHIN ATHINAI FIR/ HELLAS UIR IS 
THE REF (A) A4091/26, ISSUED BY GREECE. END PART 2 OF 2</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>26.16667,40.75,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>30.0,36.08333,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
